    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Retention: oldest retained run (none retained when absent)",
      "description": "Age of the oldest retained terminal run per phase, read live at scrape time, so it reflects what is actually retained even when a finalizer holds a run past an accepted delete request. The second target emits one NaN-valued series per phase that is retained without an age, and the third one NaN-valued series per phase with no retained run; each is a value the backend never measured, never a zero that could read as healthy, and how a dashboard renders a NaN is renderer-dependent. The phase identity of the no-retained-run state comes from the terminal counts, which carry a run's first terminal phase, while the retention series carry the current phase, so the two are not the same identity set.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
